# App version — always SemVer

The version customers see is **not** `package.json` (that stays `0.1.0`). It is the string on the profile page:

`sneltrack/app/my/profile/page.js` → `App versie: X.Y.Z`

## Always bump it

When you ship user-visible work to `test` or `main` (feature, fix, or behaviour change), bump that string in the **same PR**. Do not leave it on the previous release.

Use [SemVer](https://semver.org/): `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`

| Change | Bump | Example |
|--------|------|---------|
| Bug fix, small correction, no new capability | PATCH | `2.9.0` → `2.9.1` |
| New user-facing feature or behaviour | MINOR | `2.8.0` → `2.9.0` |
| Breaking change for users or a incompatible data/API contract | MAJOR | `2.9.0` → `3.0.0` |

Reset the lower numbers when you bump a higher one (`2.8.3` + minor → `2.9.0`).

## Do

- Read the current `App versie` first, then increment one segment
- Keep three numbers (`2.9` is written as `2.9.0`)
- Mention the new version in the commit and PR

## Don't

- Skip the bump because the change “is small”
- Bump `sneltrack/package.json` instead of (or only) the profile string
- Invent a fourth number or a date-based version
